# Cursor rules — EPM Business Rule Documentation Generator
# Full context: spec.md, architecture.md, CLAUDE.md

You are working on a Python 3.12 Streamlit app that documents Oracle EPM business rules
(Essbase/Planning calc scripts and Groovy) for EPM consultants.

## Architecture
- app.py = Streamlit UI only. Put all logic in core/.
- Pipeline: validator -> detector -> parser -> (masker) -> llm_client -> schema check -> checks -> exporters.
- core/pipeline.py orchestrates; keep that order.

## Must
- Extract exact facts (FIX blocks, members, run-time prompts) with code in core/parser_*.py, not with the LLM.
- Validate every LLM response with the Pydantic models in core/schemas.py.
- Read secrets only from environment variables (LLM_API_KEY, LLM_PROVIDER, LLM_MODEL).
- Log metadata only via core/telemetry.py (never rule text, never API keys).
- Add or update a pytest test for every logic change; tests must use the mock provider.
- Keep functions small, typed and documented; run `ruff check .` and `pytest -q`.

## Must not
- Hardcode API keys, URLs with tokens, or client data.
- Add a chatbot / free-text chat interface (the product is structured output only).
- Store rule text to disk, a database or logs.
- Call a real LLM inside tests or CI.
- Add new dependencies without updating requirements.txt and explaining why.

## Domain notes
- Calc script cross-dimensional operator "->" is NOT Groovy; detector must not treat it as such.
- FIX ... ENDFIX nest; track depth with a stack. Comments /* */ and // must not shift line numbers.
- Run-time prompts look like {Variable} in calc scripts and rtps.Variable in Groovy.
- Input limit: 2,000 lines (warning above 1,000).
